# .gitignore for the Project 1 FIFO repo (code/tb/fifo_p1)
#
# Why this file exists: an upload of the whole folder sent every file inside
# .git/ (about 200 git objects) plus about 120 regenerable logs, and the upload
# server answered each one with "502 Bad Gateway". Git never tracks its own
# .git/ folder, so for an upload, use the submission zip (it has no .git/).
# This file keeps everything that a `make` or a script can recreate out of
# the repo, so the repo and the zip stay small.
#
# Rule of thumb: commit what a person wrote (code, plans, findings, report),
# and commit the small summaries a reader checks. Do not commit what a command
# recreates in seconds or minutes from a seed and a command line.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Simulator build output (every `make SIM=icarus` recreates it)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sim_build/
sim_build_*/
results.xml
results_*.xml
obj_dir/
*.vvp
*.vcd
*.fst
*.ghw
dump.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Python caches and local virtual environments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. LaTeX build by-products (docs/REPORT.tex builds REPORT.pdf at the root)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.fls
docs/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/*.synctex.gz
docs/REPORT.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Raw per-seed run output. Each file regenerates from its seed and the
#    command in README.md, so only the summaries are committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/**/seed_*.log
results/**/seed_*.yml
results/**/*.xml
results/**/build/
results/**/sim_build_*/
# (results/closure_curve/ and results/seed4_budget/ stay tracked: closure.md
#  quotes them as evidence, and they are only a few small files)

# Graduate study scratch space (one JSON per mutant run; the scripts merge
# them into one file per seed under extension/data/, which IS committed)
extension/scratch/
extension/data/**/clean.json
extension/data/**/clean.log
extension/data/**/released__*.json
extension/data/**/own__*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Demo recording: scripts/demo.sh logs, and the video itself. The video
#    goes to YouTube, Panopto or OneDrive and DEMO.md holds the link; a
#    video file in the repo would bloat every upload and clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
demo_logs/
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
*.avi
*.cast

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Submission archives and editor or operating system clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar.gz
.direnv/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Windows adds these next to files downloaded into WSL
*:Zone.Identifier
*Zone.Identifier
